{
  "source": "Prompts/people-skills-v9.mp4",
  "duration": 142.848,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 7.58,
      "text": "Your group just finished this semester's history project, but Maya notices a problem with one of the examples and starts suggesting a change."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.26,
      "end": 12.56,
      "text": "Before she can finish, someone interrupts. We are done. No more suggestions."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.62,
      "end": 16.84,
      "text": "Maya goes quiet, and the group moves on without addressing her point."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.5,
      "end": 21.4,
      "text": "You notice that Maya's expression and body language changed. She seems hurt."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.14,
      "end": 23.52,
      "text": "What would you say or do next?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.18,
      "end": 28.82,
      "text": "For your next move, say, Maya, we didn't hear the rest of your idea. Do you want to finish?"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.44,
      "end": 34.5,
      "text": "This simple question shows her input matters. Maya actually has a valid point."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.04,
      "end": 37.8,
      "text": "The third example they included doesn't match the assignment's instructions."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.52,
      "end": 43.74,
      "text": "By giving her the floor again, the group now possesses the exact information they need to improve their work."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.34,
      "end": 47.9,
      "text": "Her idea deserves to be hurt, even if the group decides not to use it."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.48,
      "end": 55.34,
      "text": "What happened with Maya matters beyond this group project. That brings us to this graphic explaining why people's skills will matter more."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.34,
      "end": 61.12,
      "text": "First, you'll stand out. As more people use AI, polished work becomes an expectation."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.98,
      "end": 66.38,
      "text": "How you work with people helps you stand out. Second, trust still matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.1,
      "end": 71.44,
      "text": "People choose teammates and leaders who listen, keep promises, and treat others well."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.46,
      "end": 78.78,
      "text": "Finally, connection matters. AI can help with the work. People still need to feel heard, understood, and valued."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.56,
      "end": 83.26,
      "text": "You can build these skills starting today. Let's walk through four ways to practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.08,
      "end": 88.72,
      "text": "Listen to understand. Do not plan your reply while the other person is talking."
    },
    {
      "start": 89.46,
      "end": 92.76,
      "text": "Ask one genuine follow-up question before offering your opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.8,
      "end": 100.62,
      "text": "Notice what isn't being said. Pay attention to tone, hesitation, enthusiasm, and changes in behavior."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.42,
      "end": 105.74,
      "text": "If you're unsure what a change means, ask. Show people they matter."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.46,
      "end": 111.7,
      "text": "Remember what they tell you. Give specific appreciation and give people credit when an idea is theirs."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.38,
      "end": 117.22,
      "text": "Challenge ideas. Not people. Address difficult things directly and calmly."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.66,
      "end": 121.98,
      "text": "Explain the concern and suggest way forward. This example doesn't match the instructions."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.58,
      "end": 127.6,
      "text": "Could we try another? The group fixes the problem Maya noticed. What could you say to give her credit?"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.62,
      "end": 138.24,
      "text": "AI can write it. It can't be the person in the room. Listen well, speak clearly, and be someone people want to work with."
    }
  ],
